.TH SAPHIRA-INSTALL-MENU 8 "Saphira Linux" "Installer menu"
.SH NAME
saphira-install-menu \- guided text-mode installer menu (v0)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-install-menu
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR saphira-install-menu
is the v0 guided frontend of Saphira installation, run on the
installer medium's console (normally tty1 via
.IR saphira-install-menu.service ).
Using dialog menus it walks firmware, init system, root filesystem,
storage layout, role, hostname, installer networking and target
disk, writes a
.BR saphira-install-plan (5)
manifest, shows the validated plan and the engine preview, requires
two explicit destructive confirmations, then executes the existing
.BR saphira-image (8)
install-to-disk engine. v0 offers what the engine can do (ext4 on
direct partitions, base role); every other choice is presented as
explicitly-later with its reason, never silently accepted.
.PP
Credentials are never asked here and never belong in the manifest:
firstboot sets them on the installed machine. The installer USB is
excluded from target-disk selection; the chosen disk is repartitioned
destructively after confirmation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DIALOG_BIN
Menu backend (default
.BR dialog ;
the suite stubs it).
.TP
.B INSTALL_TTY
Console device (default
.IR /dev/tty1 ,
fallback
.IR /dev/console ).
The kernel command line
.B saphira.install_tty=
overrides the default the same way, so serial installs select the
serial console at boot time.
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_REPOSITORY
Package repository URL.
.SH FILES
.I /run/saphira-install.conf
(the written manifest)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-install-plan (5),
.BR saphira-image (8),
.BR saphira-firstboot (8)
